  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/graph2/). VERDICT: CURRENT. Reviewed 2026-11-01 at dev 100b6fbb6e. entrypoints.py still clamps the connectivity boost with min(1.0, ...) and sorts by (rank_score, _language_weight, _effective_out_degree); _diversity_cap is unchanged. Fixture (80 Flask routes + an Express scanner/server.js with POST /scan, GET /health): 50 entrypoints are kept, 48 http_route all at rank 1.0 and all Python; both Express routes are dropped (alone they rank 1.0); the sketch HTTP Routes section lists 48 app.py routes and no Express route. Correction: the tie-break is not pure insertion order; the second key, language weight, is what pushes the minority-language service out. MECHANISM: rank_score saturates at 1.0 for connected routes; sort ties then fall to language-dominance weight and out-degree, then insertion order, so a minority-language service's routes lose every cap/sketch slot. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: none."  # ba97
